<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech confectioner CZK 735 mln 96 net.</title>
<headline>Czech confectioner CZK 735 mln 96 net.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech confectioner Cokoladovny a.s. posted a consolidated 1996 net profit of 735 million crowns, according to preliminary figures released by the Prague Stock Exchange on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cokoladovny, majority-owned by a consortium of Swiss Nestle SA and France's Danone SA, which controls 83 percent of the company's shares, posted a 1995 consolidated net profit of 516 million crowns.  </p>
<p> Net profit	  735.285    vs    516.400</p>
<p> Gross profit    1,258.878    vs    875.911</p>
<p> Production     10,429.730    vs  9,200.262</p>
<p> Total assets    7,453.667    vs  6,479.604</p>
<p> Basic capital   3,127.701    vs  3,127.701</p>
<p>Note - Full company name is Cokoladovny a.s., the country's largest foodstuffs producer.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
